Well, I can.  I have spent a lot of time in a real-time community of
Nethack (and Sporkhack, and Crawl, and some other incidental roguelikes)
players that is significantly more populous and varied than RGRN.  I 
have seen the reaction to features in Nethack that appear inconsistent, 
and the reaction to suggested changes.  I have spoken at length to some 
of these people, and just paid attention to what others said. 

In other words, I'm out there talking to my target audience and trying
to get an idea of what _everyone_ wants to see, not just what a few
players are interested in.  And one thing that has been consistent is
that players in general DO NOT LIKE the rationalizations that are 
unfortunately part and parcel of vanilla Nethack.

If I were to add one as flagrantly obvious as "fire elementals don't
honor fire resistance now" without also redesigning the resistance model 
so that _other_ attacks throughout the game (from early to late) also 
punched through, then I would be adding to exactly the thing that players do
not want -- inconsistencies in-game that have to be _explained_ and
_rationalized_.

I'm not sure why I even have to explain this, honestly.  I can't believe
someone actually thinks that an inconsistency that leads a player to ask
"this seems weird, why is it like this", and who then must receive an 
elaborate answer from someone who's been taught the 'tribal knowledge' 
already is actually considered good design by ANYONE.

